          "source": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/e/e5/Elite_Dangerous.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=original",
          "width": 200,
          "height": 182
        },
        "pageimage": "Elite_Dangerous.png",
        "extract": "Elite Dangerous is an online space, trading, exploration and combat simulation game developed and published by Frontier Developments. The player commands a spaceship in a realistic 1:1 scale open-world representation of the Milky Way, with open-ended gameplay. Players can explore and engage with a procedurally generated galaxy, which includes around 400 billion star systems. The procedural system allows landing on planets with no or tenuous atmospheres. Many planets have special flora and fauna including alien and human settlements.\nElite Dangerous is the fourth game in the Elite series and the sequel to Frontier: First Encounters (1995). It is...",
